+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+New TypeScript library, ESM, no runtime dependencies, tests run with `node --test`. See proposal.md for motivation. Later features will build on this module.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Strict RFC 6901 behaviour, dependency-free.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- URI fragment form, mutation, JSON Patch.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Put the logic directly in `src/index.ts` (no extra module: the repo has no TypeScript compiler, and Node type-stripping cannot resolve `.js` specifiers to `.ts` files).
+- Parse the whole pointer into tokens before walking the document, so syntax errors are reported regardless of the document.
+- Only own properties count as members (`Object.hasOwn`), so `__proto__`/`constructor` never leak prototype values. Array indices must match `^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$` and be below `length`.
+- Errors: throw a `JsonPointerError` (extends `Error`) for both invalid and unresolvable pointers. Alternative: separate classes; unnecessary now.
+- Input type `unknown`; return type `unknown`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Caller passes non-JSON values (e.g. `undefined` members)] → treated as ordinary own members; out of contract.
