@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Why
+
+Services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is that standard, and later features of json-toolkit will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value an RFC 6901 pointer refers to.
+- It throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and resolving RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/index.ts` (and a pointer module), plus tests. No dependencies. No existing code affected.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (`#/a/b`), and writing/updating values.
